ANNY body model
  ANNY, a free-to-use 3D human parametric model for all ages. NAVER LABS
  Europe / NAVER Corporation. https://arxiv.org/abs/2511.03589
  Licence: Apache-2.0 code over CC0-1.0 shape assets derived from MakeHuman.
  Baked by scripts/bake_anny.py into the synthetic reference bodies; no scan of
  any person is used. ANNY's non-commercial SMPL/SMPL-X conversion data is
  never downloaded or used.

Reference data, not in any released asset
-----------------------------------------

ANSUR II anthropometric survey, public data (US Army, 2012; released 2017)
  Male: https://tools.openlab.psu.edu/publicData/ANSUR_II_MALE_Public.csv
  Female: https://tools.openlab.psu.edu/publicData/ANSUR_II_FEMALE_Public.csv
  Record: https://www.openlab.psu.edu/ansur2/
  Status: a work of the US government, so in the public domain in the US.
  It does not carry a CC BY or CC0 licence, so it is used only as a
  plausibility check: blender/fit_body.py compares body measures with its
  1st, 50th and 99th percentiles and writes them to its local report. No
  ANSUR II value goes into a GLB or any other released asset.
  SHA-256 (male): 0547aea0170e5293de519389981135e75803f02e6d40c77ace740decc0caac64
  SHA-256 (female): ed7e800aa97a4d42f8286b988be2fe1883a2e789588169db959864b707d1757a

